{
  "_id": "tg-apostasy-of-israel",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "a stiffnecked people, Ex. 32:9. ye have been rebellious against the Lord, Deut. 9:7. Because they have forsaken the covenant of the Lord, Deut. 29:25. Israel did evil … and forgat, Judg. 3:7. turn away your heart after their gods, 1 Kgs. 11:2. he placed in Beth-el the priests of the high places, 1 Kgs. 12:32 (2 Chr. 11:15). Judah did evil in the sight of the Lord, 1 Kgs. 14:22. Israel had sinned against the Lord their God, 2 Kgs. 17:7. evil … after the abominations of the heathen, 2 Kgs. 21:2. they served their idols: which were a snare unto them, Ps. 106:36. Israel doth not know, my people doth not consider, Isa. 1:3. land also is full of idols, Isa. 2:8. declare their sin as Sodom, they hide it not, Isa. 3:9. my vineyard, … brought it forth wild grapes, Isa. 5:4. Hear ye indeed, but understand not, Isa. 6:9. changed the ordinance, broken the everlasting covenant, Isa. 24:5 (D&C 1:15). draw near me with their mouth, … heart far from me, Isa. 29:13 (Mark 7:6). for your iniquities have ye sold yourselves, Isa. 50:1. your iniquities have separated between you and your God, Isa. 59:2. my people have committed two evils, Jer. 2:13. thou hast forsaken the Lord thy God, Jer. 2:17. this house … become a den of robbers in your eyes, Jer. 7:11. I called you, but ye answered not, Jer. 7:13. hearkened not … and went backward, Jer. 7:24. have ye set up altars … to burn incense unto Baal, Jer. 11:13. land is full of adulterers, Jer. 23:10. I have sent … prophets … but ye have not inclined your ear, Jer. 35:15. Israel, to a rebellious nation that hath rebelled, Ezek. 2:3. have done after the manners of the heathen, Ezek. 11:12. Her priests have violated my law, and have profaned, Ezek. 22:26. shepherds fed themselves, and fed not my flock, Ezek. 34:8. thou hast forgotten the law of thy God, Hosea 4:6. Ephraim is joined to idols, Hosea 4:17. I will send a famine … of hearing the words of the Lord, Amos 8:11. prophets … divine for money, Micah 3:11.",
